{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Your fullness.</b> The terumah of your produce, as in 'lest you sanctify the fullness of the seed that you sow.' <b>And your tears.</b> The moist matter in your terumah, such as wine and oil — so called because they drip drop by drop like tears from the winepress. In the context of terumah, the language of 'liquid' is apt, as it is written 'all fat of oil and all fat of wine,' and it is not written 'all fat of olives and all fat of grapes'; but for first fruits, where the fruit comes as it grows, the language of liquid does not apply." "<b>You shall not delay.</b> To make your portions later than your own — rather, the first you give to Me and afterward to yourself, as it is written 'the first of the first fruits of your land, the first of your dough.' Another interpretation: <b>you shall not delay</b> what you owe even if you are poor. The explanation of this commandment — it is in place of 'the first of your grain, your wine, and your oil'; therefore it is juxtaposed to 'the firstborn of your sons you give to Me,' for he is the first of his strength.'" "<b>The firstborn of your sons</b> etc. And not from the later-born. Just as I say to you regarding 'your fullness and your tears,' so shall you do for your ox and your sheep — to give Me the firstborn. Nevertheless, do not rush to offer it, but only after seven days, and let it be purified from the place of filth from which it emerged — for that is the period of purification of a menstruant, and furthermore, perhaps it is a miscarriage (nefel)."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:57.244138727Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}